# Data Licenses

The bundled datasets in this directory are sourced from third parties and
retain their upstream licenses. The project's MIT license (top-level
`LICENSE`) does NOT supersede these.

## `gem_active_faults_trimmed.geojson`

Derived from the GEM Global Active Faults Database
(https://github.com/GEMScienceTools/gem-global-active-faults).

Citation:
  Styron, R. & Pagani, M. 2020. "The GEM Global Active Faults Database."
  Earthquake Spectra 36(1_suppl): 160–180. doi:10.1177/8755293020944182

License: **CC-BY-SA 4.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)

This is a derivative work — features have been filtered (PB2002-derived
entries removed to avoid double-rendering) and the property bag has been
trimmed. Per the share-alike clause, redistributions of this file must be
under the same CC-BY-SA 4.0 license, and must include this attribution.

## `pb2002_boundaries.geojson`, `pb2002_steps_with_plates.geojson`

Derived from the PB2002 plate boundary dataset.

Citation:
  Bird, P. 2003. "An updated digital model of plate boundaries."
  Geochemistry, Geophysics, Geosystems 4(3): 1027. doi:10.1029/2001GC000252

Sourced via https://github.com/fraxen/tectonicplates (no explicit license
declared upstream; the underlying PB2002 paper is published in a peer-reviewed
journal under standard academic-citation expectations).

## `slab2_contours.geojson`, `slab2_surfaces.bin`, `slab2_surfaces.json`

Derived from USGS Slab2 (Hayes et al., 2018) — release DOI 10.5066/F7PV6JNV.
Sourced via https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/5aa1b00ee4b0b1c392e86467.

Citation:
  Hayes, G. P., Moore, G. L., Portner, D. E., Hearne, M., Flamme, H.,
  Furtney, M., & Smoczyk, G. M. (2018). "Slab2, a comprehensive subduction
  zone geometry model." Science 362(6410): 58–61. doi:10.1126/science.aat4723

`slab2_contours.geojson` is a derivative — features filtered to 8 chosen
depth contours (40/100/200/300/400/500/600/700 km) and trimmed to a
`{zone, depth_km}` property bag.

`slab2_surfaces.bin` + `slab2_surfaces.json` are also derivatives — per-zone
indexed triangle meshes built from the Slab2 `*_dep.grd` rasters at 0.1°
downsample (every 2nd grid cell), with NaN/antimeridian/depth-cap clipping.
Format is documented inline in `scripts/prep-slab2-surfaces.js`.

License (all of the above): U.S. Government work, public domain — no
attribution legally required, but the canonical citation is included
for credit.

## `bathymetry.png`

Derived from NOAA NCEI ETOPO 2022 60-arc-second bedrock elevation grid.

Citation:
  NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (2022). "ETOPO 2022
  15 Arc-Second Global Relief Model." doi:10.25921/fd45-gt74

This is a derivative work — full-resolution NetCDF grid downsampled to
720×360, applied a sqrt depth curve (emphasizes trench/abyssal contrast),
and encoded as 8-bit grayscale PNG. Land is masked to a sentinel value.
Format/process is documented inline in `scripts/prep-bathymetry.js`.

The raw NetCDF source is cached under `data/.cache/etopo_2022_60s.nc`
(gitignored — not committed; ~466 MB). Re-running `bun run prep-bathymetry`
uses the cache if present.

License: U.S. Government work, public domain — no attribution legally
required, but the canonical citation is included for credit.

## `ne_110m_land.geojson`, `ne_110m_antarctica.geojson`

Derived from Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), which is in
the public domain. No attribution required, though it is appreciated.

Sourced via https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector.
